eal phenomenon but since  we're in the world of halloween and not  the real world i'm willing to look past  that so laurie didn't want to go to  sleep because those harmful memories had  to go somewhere and some part of her  realized that it was her dreams where  the truth was hidden dr mixter ignores  her request however and sedates her when  she came too she would receive some  horrifying information making her  experiences to that point seem that much  scarier  [Music]  [Applause]  lori wakes up to a hospital employee  named jimmy who fills her in on who her  mysterious attacker was she recognizes  the name in relation to the myers house  but does not understand why michael has  chosen her to hunt jimmy is kicked out  by the charge nurse who tells lori that  they're having trouble getting in  contact with her parents because the  phones are not working as the clock  creeps into the earliest part of  november lori eventually succumbs to her  exhaustion and falls asleep sure enough  she dreams of some creepy memories from  her youth including her foster mother  refusing to tell her about her past and  the strange familiar boy looking out a  window i think her brain is slowly  putting together the pieces about who  this forgotten boy is because her  experience that evening in particular  the moment where she tore off michael's  mask is slowly kicking that part of her  brain back into gear on some level she  seems terrified by this and not wanting  to dig into her past any further she  does everything she can to stay awake  eventually resulting in her just  sleeping with her eyes wide open which  concerns the medical staff eventually  laurie wakes up i'm guessing it's right  here while the nurse is investigating a  disturbance outside between that and the  cut phone lines i guess she realized  that something was up at this hospital  and that maybe she hadn't evaded the  danger quite yet she sets up a decoy in  her bed using pillows and can we just  pause for a second