 not be  defeated however that would be as far as  he would go as laurie watches him  collapse face first for the final time  emergency services show up at the scene  that morning to put out the fire and  rescue her she's wheeled out of the  hospital to yet another ambulance news  crews try to speak with her but she  basically gives them the marshawn lynch  treatment and refuses to speak with the  media she asks to sit in the front  perhaps not wanting to relive any part  of the journey she had just been through  all in all lori strode was traumatized  by that evening's events she discovered  the deaths of her three friends nearly  lost her own life witnessed the murder  of a nurse and played a part in an  explosion that all but killed two people  i'm sure any thoughts of attending that  homecoming dance were already out the  window at this point as she would  probably be spending the next 24 hours  in another hospital but she would later  discover that ben tramer the boy she was  interested in attending the dance with  had also been killed that halloween  night maybe it is because laurie has  dealt with tragedy her entire life but  she actually moves on pretty quickly  from ben traynor and ends up getting  together with a man named mr lloyd  almost immediately there's a popular fan  theory that mr lloyd is actually jimmy  because we never learn his last name he  seems interested in her and the two  share a bond and having gone through the  most terrifying night ever together but  i can neither confirm or deny that he is  mr lloyd it's only a little over a year  later that she becomes pregnant with  their child and in either late 1980 or  early 1981 she gives birth to a daughter  named jaime i think her name goes  against the whole jimmy as mr lloyd  theory because it would just be  confusing having a household consisting  of jimmy and jamie but if that is the  case it would not have been a problem  for very long because in november of  1987 lori and jaime's father 